  "dom_id": "step-q106960",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,3,$ and $9.$",
